{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents","id":1178699,"title":"[2E] Uratha in Death Rage chasing his opponents","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-24T01:11:12-08:00","id":1178699,"title":"[2E] Uratha in Death Rage chasing his opponents","content":"So lately there was talk about making Beaten Down rules for Death Raging Uratha. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> had in it great idea to resolve problem with what to do when werewolf is in Basu-Im ( Hard Rage ) and - mechanically - you cannot done anything with it. <b>Arms</b> advised to run proper Chase for his PCs victims!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1175277-2e-homebrew-gauru\u00b4s-beaten-down-rule?p=1178186#post1178186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would just break out the CofD core book and switch from the Combat rules to the Chase rules (chase rounds are 30 seconds to 1 minute by default as a plus), and if those trying to tire the Kuruth werewolf out win the Chase (which they'll easily do in Urhan or Urshul if available, or as a teamwork action, or both) then stop rolling and just play out the rest of the time. If the Death Raging werewolf catches up, then hit combat until there's a sensible narrative point to them trying to turn it into another Chase.<br /> <br /> Ideally this would play out something like the pace of Terminator 2. The T-1000 catches up with the heroes. The T-100 and Sarah shoot at it a lot knowing they can't really stop it, but enough to hamper it until [plot device] gives them enough distance to flee. Sometimes they flee well enough to get away (for now) sometimes not and it catches up with them quickly resulting in more fruitless combat to try the next escape plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I thinking about running this kind scenario in my future games, I started this topic. Unfortunately, I was having prepared earlier Chase Rules for Uratha Forms but cannot find it on the time. So can talk more on topic, I will return later when finding my Chase Rules based on <b>CoD Rulebook</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T01:28:00-08:00","id":1178702,"title":"","content":"Wyrd, you could have just continued the discussion in the actual thread where it was being discussed. I find it difficult keeping track of the new threads you make for every random thing that catches your attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T05:02:40-08:00","id":1178727,"title":"","content":"<b>Bunyip</b>, this topic will have nothing with Beaten Down rules in any way - it will be it's own thing. Just see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T05:36:33-08:00","id":1178735,"title":"","content":"Okay, I dug up my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1075752-2e-chases-rules-from-cod-rulebook-in-wtf\">fan Chase rules for Uratha</a>. Now to compare them to Gauru Death Rage abilities... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1075752-2e-chases-rules-from-cod-rulebook-in-wtf?p=1088192#post1088192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I read more on the topic in both <b>WtF</b> 2E and <b>CoD Rulebook </b>- here is my take on the matter. Notice, if not stated otherwise, use rules from<i> Chase</i> in <b>CoD Rulebook</b>, p. 84.<br /> <br /> <b>Set the Terms:</b> Terms are calculated based on Hishu form traits.<br /> <br /> <b>Teamwork:</b> Packs often Chase together. Each participant in Chase choose side they help. Highest Dicepool in each turn for the side is Primary Actor in Chase rolls treated as Teamwork action. Chases with your Pack are much easier. \ud83d\ude0a<br /> <br /> <b>Edge:</b> Resolve Edge normally \u2013 unless the pursuer or prey is in Urhan \u2013 if in it look for the rules for this form below.<br /> <br /> <b>Form:</b> Each werewolf can declare free shifting his form for this Chase turn and use it\u2019s traits, as they take from half to one minute anyway. It <b><u>does not</u></b> change the Terms calculated on start of Chase.<br /> <br /> <b>Dicepool:</b> Uratha and Wolf-Blooded can always use their chosen Form Speed trait as Dicepool in each Chase turn, but they suffer cumulative penalty for changing dicepool, if side with Edge did not choose it ( -1 cumulative to rolls and no 10 again ) \u2013 unless they are in Urhan form, see rules below.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Forms Chase rules</b></span><br /> <br /> Those are special rules for varies form in Chase scenes.<br /> <br /> <b>Hishu: </b>Following general Hishu power <i>Sheep Clothing</i> ( <b>WtF </b>2E, p. 96 ) any Chase that is in the pursue character through crowd or populated areas suffer her Primal Urge as a penalty in turn she is in Hishu.<br /> <br /> <b>Dalu: </b>Following general Dalu power <i>Badass Motherfucker </i>( <b>WtF </b>2E, p. 96 ), when Chase his prey in crowd, werewolf in Dalu can use Presence + Primal Urge dicepool instead of normal one for Chase, without cumulative penalty.<br /> <br /> <b>Gauru: </b>Uratha cannot assume Gauru in Chase as it would instantly change it to combat. If character is still doing this, Gauru needs to roll his last time Chase Dicepool and get all the needed success. Otherwise, prey run out and need to be looked for by Tracking rules. Only Gauru is risking Basu-Im because of not satisfying Hunt and must roll Resolve + Composure \u2013 on failure Gauru enters Basu-Im, with all the consequences.<br /> <br /> <b>Urshul: </b>Following general Urshul power <i>Weaken the Prey </i>( <b>WtF </b>2E, p. 97 ), once per scene, when Urshul side get\u2019s more successes than enemy \u2013 it can give Arm Wrack, Leg Wrack, or Knocked Down Tilts to his enemy.<br /> <br /> <b>Urhan: </b>This form is perfect for foot chases. Following general Urhan power <i>Chase Down</i> ( <b>WtF </b>2E, p. 98 ), werewolf in it can freely use their Speed as Dicepool, even if side with Edge choose other Dicepool. If being in previous Chase turn in Urhan, werewolf can get Edge by paying 1 Essence. If two or more werewolves are taking this Edge by Essence, resolve by Clash of Wills rolled on their Speed dicepool.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-24-2018, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T12:59:26-07:00","id":1221240,"title":"","content":"So thinking on the matter - opponents, can be other PCs, are running away. They have Edge in normal situations. They choose dicepools. However, werewolf in Hard Rage Gauru cannot choose higher mental actions. What would be correct dicepools for them to Chase their victims, with cumulative -1 for not choosing correct Dicepool? Strength + Dexterity? Or maybe Strength + Athletics, always?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T15:33:44-07:00","id":1221284,"title":"","content":"Just from the second quote to your own shameless plug out of your own iteration of needless rules I can identify that you've no clue what 'setting a scene' means. I may be being unjust because you likely don't have enough command of English to give the published Chase rules a fair reading, and thus equate 'setup' from a gamist philosophy and not from the dramatic one.<br /> <br /> Here's how I run trying to escape from a Gauru in the throes of Death Rage: You take Urhan whilst praying to Luna this mofo doesn't has Predator's Unmatched Pursuit which would enable you to run circles around them. If they do have PUP, things may go more interesting. Without taking into account collateral damage, obviously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T22:55:10-07:00","id":1221390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents?p=1221284#post1221284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's how I run trying to escape from a Gauru in the throes of Death Rage: You take Urhan whilst praying to Luna this mofo doesn't has Predator's Unmatched Pursuit which would enable you to run circles around them. If they do have PUP, things may go more interesting. Without taking into account collateral damage, obviously.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is <i>Predator's Unmatched Pursuit</i>? I cannot find it in the 2E corebook. Do you not meant <i>Chase Down</i> power from Urhan?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents?p=1221284#post1221284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just from the second quote to your own shameless plug out of your own iteration of needless rules I can identify that you've no clue what 'setting a scene' means. I may be being unjust because you likely don't have enough command of English to give the published Chase rules a fair reading, and thus equate 'setup' from a gamist philosophy and not from the dramatic one.</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;Snark I will gladly silence on&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T22:58:01-07:00","id":1221392,"title":"","content":"Gift of Strength, Glory Facet, pg. 132 Werewolf 2E Core","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T09:20:45-07:00","id":1221483,"title":"","content":"(Edit: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> It's not snark. I'm sincere in my notion you do not dominate enough of the language to give the game as written a fair reading, which is why I suspect you can't consider these simple issues.)<br /> <br /> The thing about unleashed Kuruth in order of dramatic importance as I see it follow this pyramid:<br /> <br /> 1) Will I be liable to join in on the frenzy? Did I join in on the frenzy? Now I have to investigate what the hell happened. Who died. Whom did I ate.<br /> <br /> 2) If not, will there be collateral damage? What about damage to the Oath? Witnesses, Lunacy liable to cause Mortals to become easier prey to spirits (I'm looking at the reception condition). Is there evidence something supernatural happened that I ought to erase (such as video footage)? Can I cut the frenzy short? Do I have to have my whole pack savage the mindless Uratha in the hopes of killing him quick enough as to prevent regeneration? Am I alone with it and would need to resort to cannibalism, or if I was prepared, silver?<br /> <br /> All of the above questions IMO, matter way, way more than rolling dice to see if the big bad wolf caught you or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 05-23-2018, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T09:34:46-07:00","id":1221486,"title":"","content":"Okay, reading <i>Predator's Unmatched Pursuit </i>I can certinly see why it would be used by those having it to run away in Chase. But question would be other - What would use Uratha in Death Rage as dicepool to roll? In Basu-Im character is limited to only simple actions, related to attacking.<br /> <br /> <i>'While in Basu-Im, the werewolf ignores wound penalties, and any attempts to influence, intimidate, or otherwise change the Uratha\u2019s course of action by mundane or supernatural means suffer twice the werewolf\u2019s Primal Urge as a penalty. This is over and above any Supernatural Tolerance (p. 160) applied to supernatural powers.'</i><br /> <br /> So as to choosing the Dicepool from Chase rules in <b>CoD Rulebook</b>:<br /> <br /> <i>'If you can\u2019t easily determine who has the Edge at a given moment, make a contested roll. Usually, this will be based on Wits or Dexterity. The relevant Skill should relate to the context. Often, this will be Athletics, Streetwise, Survival, or similar. Don\u2019t be limited; let characters lean on their areas of expertise when possible.'</i><br /> <br /> But then we have a problem with simplification of thought processes in Basu-Im. Should not raging Uratha simply take to roll his Dexterity + Athletics? The Speed dicepool is locked for Urhan and Basu-Im is only limited to Gauru.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T09:48:14-07:00","id":1221489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents?p=1221483#post1221483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of the above questions IMO, matter way, way more than rolling dice to see if the big bad wolf caught you or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I do not agree with you here. As Death Rage is not some meta-existing plot resolution - <i>some</i> scenes just cannot go with Fade to Black policy. Examples - you fight with Pure, you hurt one of them enough he goes into Basu-Im, whole pack join him in Rage. They will find you if you not run away. Considering then Oath breaches, moral implications and all a like is not really doing fair service to the enemy you have here. You have a bestial, mad werewolves after you - running Chase scene then seems<b> crucial to the survival of your character</b>. Axing scene with 'And we wake up 5 minutes later' is cheapening the scene for players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-23-2018, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T10:01:16-07:00","id":1221492,"title":"","content":"Here's the dilemma you seem to be vaulting over, which I'll try again to depict:<br /> <br /> Urhan can -easily- outrun a Gauru, unless he's equipped with PUP, as previously stated (you glossed this over probably because I used the 'running circles around them' phrase, which basically means they're stupidly faster than the average Gauru, say, not unlike a human and a turtle competing on a race: the person can run circles around the turtle multiple times along it's course and still win, easily.)<br /> <br /> The issue is one of detachment versus duty: Do you risk your (and your pack's) skin against a most relentless foe in pursuit of one's duty to keep the Herd from potentially knowing, and causing all manner of spiritual disruption; or do you simply escape and try to run damage control in the aftermath?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T15:08:28-07:00","id":1221554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents?p=1221486#post1221486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But question would be other - What would use Uratha in Death Rage as dicepool to roll? In Basu-Im character is limited to only simple actions, related to attacking.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're overthinking this. They roll whatever the rolls is, because the limitation from Basu-Im doesn't apply. They're rolling to close on their targets so they can attack them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents?p=1221492#post1221492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Urhan can -easily- outrun a Gauru, unless he's equipped with PUP, as previously stated (you glossed this over probably because I used the 'running circles around them' phrase, which basically means they're stupidly faster than the average Gauru, say, not unlike a human and a turtle competing on a race: the person can run circles around the turtle multiple times along it's course and still win, easily.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You're overstating this significantly. Urhan has a +1 Speed advantage over Gauru. Urshul (the best Speed boost) is only a +3 advantage. These are well within the ranges of what different characters might have based on their other Traits.<br /> <br /> An Uratha with base Strength 3/Dexterity 3 and Fleet of Foot 2 in Gauru, is going to outrun an Uratha with the same base stats without the Merit in Urhan.<br /> <br /> This isn't a human vs. a turtle, and even if it was, wyrdhamster's desire to play out the drama of being chased by a werewolf in Kuruth is a valid thing even if it isn't what you'd personally focus on. Also:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The issue is one of detachment versus duty: Do you risk your (and your pack's) skin against a most relentless foe in pursuit of one's duty to keep the Herd from potentially knowing, and causing all manner of spiritual disruption; or do you simply escape and try to run damage control in the aftermath? </div> </div> </div>None of this is excluded from using the Chase rules here. One of the big reasons why I like the idea of using the Chase rules, is that maintaining the Edge means the group being chased can use the Edge to manipulate the course of events. The Chase rules are more than just a foot-race, they include doing things like taking advantage of the terrain towards your advantage. Do you rely on your raw speed advantage to hold and lead the Kuruth werewolf away from the Herd? Or do you risk the narrow back alleys to impede the unthinking rage for a greater advantage, but risk being seen?<br /> <br /> There's plenty of room for both sides of the coin here. You can have the visceral drama of running for your life, and the cerebral drama of choices and consequences for how you go about not getting ripped to shreds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T16:04:06-07:00","id":1221563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents?p=1221554#post1221554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're overthinking this. They roll whatever the rolls is, because the limitation from Basu-Im doesn't apply. They're rolling to close on their targets so they can attack them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You're overstating this significantly. Urhan has a +1 Speed advantage over Gauru. Urshul (the best Speed boost) is only a +3 advantage. These are well within the ranges of what different characters might have based on their other Traits.<br /> <br /> An Uratha with base Strength 3/Dexterity 3 and Fleet of Foot 2 in Gauru, is going to outrun an Uratha with the same base stats without the Merit in Urhan.<br /> <br /> This isn't a human vs. a turtle, and even if it was, wyrdhamster's desire to play out the drama of being chased by a werewolf in Kuruth is a valid thing even if it isn't what you'd personally focus on. Also:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> None of this is excluded from using the Chase rules here. One of the big reasons why I like the idea of using the Chase rules, is that maintaining the Edge means the group being chased can use the Edge to manipulate the course of events. The Chase rules are more than just a foot-race, they include doing things like taking advantage of the terrain towards your advantage. Do you rely on your raw speed advantage to hold and lead the Kuruth werewolf away from the Herd? Or do you risk the narrow back alleys to impede the unthinking rage for a greater advantage, but risk being seen?<br /> <br /> There's plenty of room for both sides of the coin here. You can have the visceral drama of running for your life, and the cerebral drama of choices and consequences for how you go about not getting ripped to shreds.</div> </div> </div> </div>The speed in Urhan only matters because it becomes their dice pool, plain and simple. With all stats being equal in your example, the Uratha in Kuruth will be rolling (on an average of Athletics 2 and Stamina 2 for both participants) 6 dice to chase the the Urhan, while the Urhan will have a whooping 12. That's double the other one's dice pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 05-23-2018, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T16:12:06-07:00","id":1221566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents?p=1221563#post1221563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The speed in Urhan only matters because it becomes their dice pool, plain and simple. With all stats being equal in your example, the Uratha in Kuruth will be rolling (on an average of Athletics 2 and Stamina 2 for both participants) 6 dice to chase the the Urhan, while the Urhan will have a whooping 12. That's double the other one's dice pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd make a quip about your reading skills compared to wyrd's, but that would imply you'd actually read the chase rules in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T16:19:30-07:00","id":1221570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents?p=1221566#post1221566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd make a quip about your reading skills compared to wyrd's, but that would imply you'd actually read the chase rules in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're running from an <u>unreasonable</u> monster with twice or more their potential dice-pool to finish the contest in your favor. Why would you pick any contest that'd give them the edge on it, or even, how would said unreasonable beast even know how to do something beyond rampaging around in order to take the edge itself?<br /> <br /> Give me a break.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T16:34:12-07:00","id":1221572,"title":"","content":"It doesn't &quot;become their dice pool, plain and simple,&quot; because that power only refers to foot chases, not everything the Chase rules can cover. Wyrdammer's house rules does extend things, but RAW if the side with the Edge in a Chase changes the dice pool to something other than Stamina + Athletics, the Urhan would loose that advantage, or lose 10-again, suffer and suffer a cumulative -1 penalty each time they do.<br /> <br /> Even with a dice advantage, Chases have a target number of successes you need to hit before you catch/escape, and which can be modified significantly in either direction, so there's all that to take into account. 6 dice vs 11 (not 12 btw) sucks in a direct roll off... but it's neck and neck if 6 dice trying to get 4 successes, and 11 dice trying to get 7 successes. We're talking the full 2e core Chase rules, not the basic foot chase rules.<br /> <br /> I also don't like the assumption that &quot;on average&quot; an Uratha is going to have Stamina 2, Athletics 2, since both are fairly valuable to them. And if you're fighting NPCs... there is no average here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T17:19:31-07:00","id":1221578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents?p=1221572#post1221572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't &quot;become their dice pool, plain and simple,&quot; because that power only refers to foot chases, not everything the Chase rules can cover. Wyrdammer's house rules does extend things, but RAW if the side with the Edge in a Chase changes the dice pool to something other than Stamina + Athletics, the Urhan would loose that advantage, or lose 10-again, suffer and suffer a cumulative -1 penalty each time they do.<br /> <br /> Even with a dice advantage, Chases have a target number of successes you need to hit before you catch/escape, and which can be modified significantly in either direction, so there's all that to take into account. 6 dice vs 11 (not 12 btw) sucks in a direct roll off... but it's neck and neck if 6 dice trying to get 4 successes, and 11 dice trying to get 7 successes. We're talking the full 2e core Chase rules, not the basic foot chase rules.<br /> <br /> I also don't like the assumption that &quot;on average&quot; an Uratha is going to have Stamina 2, Athletics 2, since both are fairly valuable to them. And if you're fighting NPCs... there is no average here.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, you introduced the averages. You want me to quote the chase rules? Let's go right the heck along.<br /> <br /> The Gauru's motivation is quite simply, to get their hands into something to maul to death. I doesn't even has to be your character. It could be an innocent bystander. The old adage you don't have to outrun the bear, just the camper around you applies, then.<br /> <br /> Who gets the edge?<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;</i><i>At the beginning of every turn, the side with the Edge determines the terms of that turn.<b> At Storyteller discretion</b>, the side with the Edge determines the dice pool for the chase that turn, and makes the first roll.&quot;</i> This means that a Gauru is solely limited to chasing, or throwing objects to those he chases to hamper their escape. That's the entirety of their mental faculties in Kuruth.<i> &quot;As the context changes from turn to turn, the character with more ability to maneuver has the Edge, and can temporarily control the flow of the chase.</i>&quot; What's more maneuverable? Urhan or Gauru? Which one is the IQ deficient brute beast? Don't answer it's rhetorical. I ask again: why pick a context that is unfavorable unless you're trying to save some helpless bystander(s)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T20:10:50-07:00","id":1221603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents?p=1221578#post1221578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, you introduced the averages.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I didn't. I introduced a sample reasonable set of stats a starting character might have to counter your assertion that the Urhan advantage in foot-chases makes them so insanely fast that they're no point in ever bothering with breaking out the Chase rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You want me to quote the chase rules? </div> </div> </div>Only if you are going to do so to make a salient point. You treated the &quot;use Speed as dice-pool&quot; as an unbeatable trump card, I used the full Chase rules to demonstrate why that isn't the case. You're not making much of a point here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Gauru's motivation is quite simply, to get their hands into something to maul to death. I doesn't even has to be your character. It could be an innocent bystander. The old adage you don't have to outrun the bear, just the camper around you applies, then. </div> </div> </div>Right... so this goes right back to my whole point where rolling out the Chase doesn't remove the drama you felt was more important to focus on. Engaging in the Chase could be to lead the Kuruth suffering werewolf into a stray human to die while you get away, ending the Chase after however long that takes assuming you don't just escape freely first, or could be to purposefully lead said werewolf around away from people which means being careful with what territory and terrain you use; possibly to your disadvantage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Who gets the edge? </div> </div> </div>This is very much a &quot;it depends&quot; in this circumstance. Urhan doesn't have an inherent greater mobility in the context of the Edge subheader (it gives examples such as giving the Edge to a pedestrian in a crowded street over a car where the car's speed doesn't matter compared to it's size in the environment). Maybe Urhan has an advantage because there's a tight enough terrain complication that the larger Gauru is less able to move with ease. Maybe Gauru as the advantage because it's a very rock strewn field where the Gauru's hands allow for far greater stability and size lets it vault over what the Urhan has to run around. Maybe the Gauru has the advantage based on instinctively knowing the territory as the one that lives there even if they're in Kuruth.<br /> <br /> Or there isn't an obvious option, and you roll it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This means that a Gauru is solely limited to chasing, or throwing objects to those he chases to hamper their escape. </div> </div> </div>Not chasing. Moving towards. Moving can be Strength or Dexterity based easily, making it not Stamina + Athletics and therefore removing the RAW Urhan dice advantage (if they even have one).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which one is the IQ deficient brute beast? Don't answer it's rhetorical. </div> </div> </div>And it's bad rhetoric because IQ doesn't matter. As well, portraying Kuruth as stupid is doing it a complete disservice. It's mono-focused on killing and maiming, it doesn't mean it isn't going to hunt like the monstrous hunter it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I ask again: why pick a context that is unfavorable unless you're trying to save some helpless bystander(s)? </div> </div> </div>This is less of &quot;again&quot; and more, &quot;trying to make it look like I'm repeating a question when I'm actually shifting the goal posts.&quot;<br /> <br /> And it doesn't matter. Breaking out the Chase rules is setting a framework to the scene, not dictating how it plays out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T02:36:13-07:00","id":1221636,"title":"","content":"I mean, I could be the wrong person to ask, but why run from the gauru when you can also take that form? It evens the playing field, and you have time before death rage takes you, and you probably have more willpower at this stage of the fight. What good werewolf, with sense that extend literal miles, is going to get ambushed into facing a pack of pure? You are the hunter, not the hunted. If you have let it happen, and become the prey, you're probably dead because you're likely facing a whole pack. And you just sent them all into death rage. That means you're outrunning multiple murderous death machines, alone, which is about as likely as you being in a race car with a full tank of gas when it happens. You weren't winning this fight from the start, and you've only made it worse.<br /> <br /> If it's you one on one with an enemy gauru, grappling rules are the most effective method for detaining a single opponent. Go gauru and go right back at them, pin them, and either hold them until it's over or eat them. If you are a terrible grappler, you better have silver ammunition or a silver weapon. With luck, you'll at least be able to get an arm wrack, or a wound penalty in before the grapple, or maybe a leg wrack. Note: don't go for Blind. All werewolves ignore that because your other senses let you daredevil.<br /> <br /> If you have no notable combat skill, you are not likely to also have a high athletics skill, physical attributes, fleet of foot, or parkour, which I notice no one here has mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T04:38:05-07:00","id":1221653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents?p=1221603#post1221603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost twice someone else's dicepool isn't a huge advantage then? I happen to disagree on what is a 'reasonable' dicepool and average it to -professional- stats, and you think it's unreasonable. Alrighty then.<br /> <br /> Discussing the terms in a white-room scenario is useless, because you can keep throwing examples such as &quot;what if this is happening in a barren mountain range, or, what if there's a alley full of homeless!&quot; what if indeed. My only point is: if your sole motivation is to escape, doing so is stupidly easy, to the point calling it a chase is disingeneious.<br /> <br /> Regarding who gets the edge? I plain and simply disagree. I mean, look at your proposals to give Gauru it by default. C'on. You're just straining things up to<br /> <br /> &quot;Moving towards&quot; based on strength? Is the Gauru climbing a surface vertically? fighting a gale of wind? Oh what if everything is on fire! What if indeed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T08:43:46-07:00","id":1221720,"title":"","content":"During the first turn of a chase it's likely to be a roll-off to set the edge, using best pools from both sides. This is because while urshul or urhan are better at running, an uratha in death rage isn't going to care about how it goes through things to get at its target--but it will do so cunningly and expeditiously, and probably in a manner appropriate to auspice.<br /> <br /> Thanks to gauru stamina, the pursued will have at least 7 successes (5 base + 2 opponent cannot tire) to evade, probably more thanks to senses, and the rules indicate that this number may fluctuate during the chase. Further, both parties should be attempting to seize the edge during each turn.<br /> <br /> But really, step back a moment: if you're looking to run from a pack of ravening, death-raging werewolves, regardless of the flee-ee's form or nature, the first question the ST should answer is &quot;do I want the merciless death-predators to just end this character?&quot; If the answer is anything beyond &quot;meh, sure&quot; then the chase scene is there for dramatic tension and to see if you care what the dice tell you.<br /> <br /> I put it this way because once everyone's in death rage except a runner, either you're at a planned script point, or there has been a grave miscalculation and as ST you're deciding how to salvage the situation/campaign. If all the PCs are raging, that's another matter and you can resolve the question of &quot;does my NPC live&quot; with a few dice rolls behind a screen and a fade to black.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> PS. It <b><i>is</i></b> unfortunate that the game line all about chasing down prey does not hook into the GMC chase rules--that would make things simpler.<br /> <br /> PPS. It is <b><i>also</i></b> a trivial matter to scrape a <i>basu-im</i> werewolf off your tail. Run past anything else that's meat (or, I assume, a meat-substitute in the Hisil). The impulse is to kill and destroy, not to hunt a specific prey. If you're in the wilderness or someplace where you won't come across other targets, then sure, you can lead around your kuruth-ing pals until their timers finish and they black out. Otherwise, succeeding in the chase may be represented as tripping the pizza boy as you run past....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 05-24-2018, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T09:51:43-07:00","id":1221740,"title":"","content":"I'd also just like to add that RAW an Urhan can use stamina + athletics (and therefore speed) even if the person who has the edge has determined a different pool, since the only deterrent for that is a dice penalty (no 10-again and a dice penalty), and usually even with that the speed pool is still preferable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T17:11:58-07:00","id":1221887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents?p=1221636#post1221636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I could be the wrong person to ask, but why run from the gauru when you can also take that form? It evens the playing field, and you have time before death rage takes you, and you probably have more willpower at this stage of the fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you're throwing Agg attacks out there, because it's not really worth it? The shortest Basu-Im duration is 10 minutes, or around 200 combat turns. You're not holding Gauru long enough without going into Kuruth yourself before you run out of the ability to equal things out like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What good werewolf, with sense that extend literal miles, is going to get ambushed into facing a pack of pure? You are the hunter, not the hunted. </div> </div> </div>There's also sorts of context from other threads one the situation that spawned the discussion on mechanically switching to the Chase system for handling dealing with Kuruth without killing the death raging werewolf.<br /> <br /> Also, the Pure are hunters too. The idea that Forsaken never become the prey is a bit silly when there are plenty of things in the game that (try to) hunt them. It's not always about 'letting' it happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it's you one on one with an enemy gauru, grappling rules are the most effective method for detaining a single opponent. Go gauru and go right back at them, pin them, and either hold them until it's over or eat them. </div> </div> </div>Again, time is not on your side here. You don't have a lot of it before you're going to have to leave Gauru and grappling gets a lot harder. And &quot;eat them&quot; isn't going to do much since they'll be healing all bashing and lethal damage you to unless you can do enough to wrap around into Agg (which is also void Tilts not inflicted with Agg).<br /> <br /> Death rage also negates wound penalties regardless of source.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you have no notable combat skill, you are not likely to also have a high athletics skill, physical attributes, fleet of foot, or parkour, which I notice no one here has mentioned. </div> </div> </div>So... an traceur that becomes a werewolf is unrealistic? It seems pretty easy to have a concept where high Athletics, physicals Attributes and Merits, and all that without being a character that's combat focused (though werewolves should be getting combat stuff pretty fast). I also mentioned Fleet of Foot earlier (though as I applied it to the pursuer, so the penalty aspect didn't matter, just the higher Speed impacting the successes needed for a chase).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents?p=1221653#post1221653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Almost twice someone else's dicepool isn't a huge advantage then?</div> </div> </div> </div>In this specific context? Not inherently, because number of successes matters, and isn't equal. Double the dice-pool when you need double the successes isn't a huge advantage.<br /> <br /> If it was just 6 dice vs. 11 dice? 11 dice is a massive advantage. As I pointed out earlier, if it's 6 dice to get 4 success vs. 11 dice to get 7 successes... it's not a huge advantage. It's a small one well within variation to go to either side.<br /> <br /> How about a different example on this specific issue:<br /> <br /> An experienced hunter (so not subject to the Down &amp; Dirty Combat power of the Gauru form) took on a pack of werewolves and has wiped out all of them but one, but is out of silver weapons. Now, stuck with just a combat knife, is facing off against a Kuruth last survivor of the pack. In Kuruth, the lone survivor all-out-attacks each round. It turns out that with that in mind, the Hunter is rolling 11 dice to attack, and the werewolf is rolling 6 dice after dealing with the Hunter's defense.<br /> <br /> Who wins?<br /> <br /> My money is on the werewolf. They're healing all the damage the Hunter can deal every round baring an insanely lucky roll, have enough dice to hit and deal damage every round even if not a killing blow worthy one. And the Hunter can't regenerate. So that &quot;almost double&quot; advantage isn't enough.<br /> <br /> The Chase system isn't as complex as combat, but the same logic applies. You can't just look at the dice-pools and say who's going to win reliably. You need context, you need to see how many successes need to get rolled, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Discussing the terms in a white-room scenario is useless,... </div> </div> </div>No fucking kidding! The Chase rules are explicitly ones you can't white-room scenario. The Chase rules say what happens in a white-room: the higher Speed character wins without rolling anything (and in my hypothetical that means the Gauru, not the Urhan), because in a white room it's just who can run the fastest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My only point is: if your sole motivation is to escape, doing so is stupidly easy, to the point calling it a chase is disingeneious. </div> </div> </div>And your point is flat out <b>WRONG</b> and it has been thoroughly countered, refuted, and misusing words like disingenuous isn't helping your case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Regarding who gets the edge? I plain and simply disagree. </div> </div> </div>Then you're disagreeing with the books, so why should any of us care?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, look at your proposals to give Gauru it by default. C'on. </div> </div> </div>C'mon dude, you really thing this bullshit says anything other than, &quot;I lost an Internet debate, but I don't want to admit it, so I'm going to condescendingly double down and try to paint the other guy as an unreasonable asshat!&quot; or do you have a point you're like to make in a less specious fashion?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents?p=1221720#post1221720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I put it this way because once everyone's in death rage except a runner, either you're at a planned script point, or there has been a grave miscalculation and as ST you're deciding how to salvage the situation/campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given how hair-trigger werewolves can be with triggers and Kuruth, sometimes it can also just be rage fucking things up without it being planned or miscalculated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> PS. It <b><i>is</i></b> unfortunate that the game line all about chasing down prey does not hook into the GMC chase rules--that would make things simpler. </div> </div> </div>Yes, though the developers have repeatedly pointed out that the earlier 2e core books were based off the GMC rules (which don't include Chases) not the CofD 2e core book rules (where they first appear) because the expanded systems weren't actually out yet and all. So that's just timing. I do wish we'd get some errata or FAQ for VtR 2e, WtF 2e, and DtD for these things though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> PPS. It is <b><i>also</i></b> a trivial matter to scrape a <i>basu-im</i> werewolf off your tail. Run past anything else that's meat (or, I assume, a meat-substitute in the Hisil). The impulse is to kill and destroy, not to hunt a specific prey. If you're in the wilderness or someplace where you won't come across other targets, then sure, you can lead around your kuruth-ing pals until their timers finish and they black out. Otherwise, succeeding in the chase may be represented as tripping the pizza boy as you run past.... </div> </div> </div>Yes and no? I mean, leading a Kuruth werewolf into other prey will delay them and might tweak things in your favor enough to escape, but random humans are going to die in 3 seconds out of a 30 second to 1 minute Chase round. That seems justification to increase the pursuit successes needed (under the 'head start' entries)... so unless there's a lot of alternate prey in the path, it might not be an automatic end to the Chase.<br /> <br /> And there's the ethical questions about doing that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents?p=1221740#post1221740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also just like to add that RAW an Urhan can use stamina + athletics (and therefore speed) even if the person who has the edge has determined a different pool, since the only deterrent for that is a dice penalty (no 10-again and a dice penalty), and usually even with that the speed pool is still preferable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahem. Post #17.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T02:40:48-07:00","id":1221974,"title":"","content":"Which is why I specified eating, or silver, your two sources of ag damage against a wolf.<br /> <br /> And yes I am aware that the pure are nearly as much a hunter as you, the protagonists. You and they have competing levels of senses, but the note that you've sent the enemy into death rage implies that you have advantage in this situation.<br /> <br /> And I did note the situation in which this does occur what your actions should look like. The theory of being alone against a single pure, or being substantially outnumbered by them means you shouldn't have let yourself get into this situation. If the latter is true, death is a likely outcome unless you use the appropriate force multipliers- like silver, and tactics. You are a hunter. Always have a plan to turn the chase on your foe, and when dealing with the pure, you should always be prepared for the eventuality they will be turn the hunt on you. You're dealing with intelligent, powerful prey. That's why Blood Talons claim other werewolves as their sacred prey. Know your enemy, know your hunting ground, and know victory.<br /> <br /> And yes, I'm aware of the death rage timer. However, entering rage and winning is superior to dying. That said, if you win three rounds of grapple, and utilize the restraining manouvers, you can pretty safely downshift, and be patient.<br /> <br /> You could have a niche character like that. Thus why I said unlikely, not impossible, and in that case I hope you invested in a silver throwing knife set, because Athletics becomes your combat skill in this case. The wolf must hunt, and not having some form of combat skill makes you a liability.<br /> <br /> So yea. When dealing with death rage, be prepared to fight, or die.<br /> <br /> As a side note, if your ST has invented a situation in which you have no choice but to run, use wolf form gauru is +2 size, wolf form is -1. This is your final tactical advantage. Without shield breaker or an equivalent, your for will not be able to follow you through small areas. However, the intent in such a contrived situation is likely for you to lose this chase anyway, and be either captured, saved by an npc, or flat out killed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, my advice is to be taken with a pinch of salt. I've obviously had some bad STs in my time, and have developed into a &quot;have a plan to kill everyone in the room&quot; type of player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T06:16:03-07:00","id":1222002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents?p=1221887#post1221887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless you're throwing Agg attacks out there, because it's not really worth it? The shortest Basu-Im duration is 10 minutes, or around 200 combat turns. You're not holding Gauru long enough without going into Kuruth yourself before you run out of the ability to equal things out like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>And once you go into Kuruth you and the Pure or whomever are going to go off and make a mess of something, somewhere, until you wake up (at about the same time) shakey and sticky and wishing it was just a carnal encounter behind you....<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents?p=1221887#post1221887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An experienced hunter (so not subject to the Down &amp; Dirty Combat power of the Gauru form) took on a pack of werewolves and has wiped out all of them but one, but is out of silver weapons. Now, stuck with just a combat knife, is facing off against a Kuruth last survivor of the pack. In Kuruth, the lone survivor all-out-attacks each round. It turns out that with that in mind, the Hunter is rolling 11 dice to attack, and the werewolf is rolling 6 dice after <i><b>dealing with the Hunter's defense.</b></i></div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure Defense goes away until the experienced hunter has some kind of supernatural way of maintaining it. My understanding from the book is that even other Uratha lose their Defense versus Gauru form.<br /> <br /> Correct me if wrong, please.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents?p=1221887#post1221887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who wins?<br /> <br /> My money is on the werewolf. They're healing all the damage the Hunter can deal every round baring an insanely lucky roll, have enough dice to hit and deal damage every round even if not a killing blow worthy one. And the Hunter can't regenerate. So that &quot;almost double&quot; advantage isn't enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>The werewolf only has to land a few 1-success shots before the hunter goes into lethal wound penalties, and even if they can stay conscious they have to inflict 200 rounds of statistically improbable failure on the Uratha before it falls out of Kuruth and can be dispatched. I like me some epic fights something fierce, but you'd need to hand the hunter a serious damage edge, plus armor, to make survival possible.<br /> <br /> I, uh, actually ran this exact fight, with observations in another thread on this forum.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents?p=1221887#post1221887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how hair-trigger werewolves can be with triggers and Kuruth, sometimes it can also just be rage fucking things up without it being planned or miscalculated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Natch. Or as they say with other systems: &quot;crit happens.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents?p=1221887#post1221887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, though the developers have repeatedly pointed out that the earlier 2e core books were based off the GMC rules (which don't include Chases) not the CofD 2e core book rules (where they first appear) because the expanded systems weren't actually out yet and all. So that's just timing. I do wish we'd get some errata or FAQ for VtR 2e, WtF 2e, and DtD for these things though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was not aware there were actual differences between GMC and CofD 2e core. But yes, it would be great if maybe Contagion Chronicle brought the splats in line with available mechanics?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents?p=1221887#post1221887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes and no? I mean, leading a Kuruth werewolf into other prey will delay them and might tweak things in your favor enough to escape, but random humans are going to die in 3 seconds out of a 30 second to 1 minute Chase round. That seems justification to increase the pursuit successes needed (under the 'head start' entries)... so unless there's a lot of alternate prey in the path, it might not be an automatic end to the Chase.<br /> <br /> And there's the ethical questions about doing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed! (to both points)<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T11:15:33-07:00","id":1222088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents?p=1221974#post1221974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes I am aware that the pure are nearly as much a hunter as you, the protagonists. You and they have competing levels of senses, but the note that you've sent the enemy into death rage implies that you have advantage in this situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pure are just as much hunters as the Uratha. They're all werewolves, they all must hunt.<br /> <br /> And no, sending the enemy into Kuruth doesn't imply you have advantage in this situation, it means that the stakes of the situation have gone in a very specific direction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...means you shouldn't have let yourself get into this situation. </div> </div> </div>You keep saying this like characters have complete control of their situations at all times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, entering rage and winning is superior to dying. </div> </div> </div>As noted entering normal rage isn't going to make sure you win, and going into death rage isn't 'winning' even if it might be survival.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, if you win three rounds of grapple, and utilize the restraining manouvers, you can pretty safely downshift, and be patient. </div> </div> </div>Erm... no? You need to use restraining equipment to exit a grapple with the target restrained and expecting cuffs to stop a death raging werewolf seems questionable; especially since they can still move their legs and bite you unless you're carrying around a lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When dealing with death rage, be prepared to fight, or die. </div> </div> </div>The whole point of all of this is that 'flight' is also an option, but you have to be smart about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents?p=1222002#post1222002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if wrong, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I messed that up. I was trying to come up with a way to keep it 6 vs 11 for the direct comparison without the Kuruth-werewolf having a ridiculously bad set of stats, since otherwise the ~double dice-pool size would require an insanely maxed opponent.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T12:48:23-07:00","id":1222106,"title":"","content":"The forsaken have a singular advantage in this case, which is moon gifts. And yes, basu-im first.means your timer is running first. That is your advantage.<br /> <br /> And if your players don't have control over their actions and situations, I'm not sure how you play the game.<br /> <br /> Survival is winning. And the opponent death rage first.means you have a time advantage.<br /> <br /> Restrain does not only imply outside forces. It specifically includes options such as a joint lock. It is a condition- it can be applied many ways.<br /> <br /> And yes. I'm saying while flight is theoretically an option, it's your worst option by far, even in a 1v1 scenario. Unless your character has been completely gimped of resources, or is otherwise entirely incapable of handling the situation- in which case, you are likely dead or going into cinematic mode.<br /> <br /> Sorry about not multiquoting you in responses, but I'm working via phone here, and am horribly too lazy to retype the information to do each section. Please forgive me for that. I understand your points, I just disagree with the premise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8122,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","user":"ArchonAres","date":". 05-25-2018, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T20:54:50-07:00","id":1222155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents?p=1222106#post1222106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The forsaken have a singular advantage in this case, which is moon gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorta? Pure have their own (though we need a 2e update for a lot of them). The Moon Gifts don't have a lot of powers that directly relate here though. The Pure have access to stealth Gifts and such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yes, basu-im first.means your timer is running first. That is your advantage. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean. Though in either case that presumes equal Primal Urge and all. Whoever you mean it getting the advantage here, if one has a 30 minute Basu-Im and the other 10-minutes... first is a pretty big window (yes, I know PU 1 to 2 vs PU 5 has a lot of other implications besides that).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if your players don't have control over their actions and situations, I'm not sure how you play the game. </div> </div> </div>Players have control over their character's actions (most of the time, esp. with all this talk of Kuruth and all), but they don't get to dictate everything about a their situations. They don't get to say, &quot;No, the Pure we're facing don't have that a trigger, so they don't risk death rage.&quot; The whole job of the ST is to set the situation in a fashion that's interesting, challenging and fun for the players.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Survival is winning. </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure most werewolves, and most humans for that matter, would argue that there's a lot of things where personal survival isn't winning. Going on a murder spree with a Pure isn't high on most Forsaken's wish lists of things to do if they can avoid it; especially if your Pack's wolf-blooded are nearby.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Restrain does not only imply outside forces. It specifically includes options such as a joint lock. It is a condition- it can be applied many ways. </div> </div> </div>Restrain ends if you let go unless you apply an appropriate device. A joint-lock only lasts until you let the arm go, where slapping cuffs on someone keeps their arms restrained after you let go.<br /> <br /> 2e doesn't have a &quot;three turns and the opponent is done&quot; in the Restrain move, and Restrain doesn't bar the target from Breaking Free from a grapple (it's, in fact, the only thing they can do in a grapple if Restrained)... so shifting down is a really bad idea unless you massively outclass the Gauru in grappling (and then you didn't need to go Gauru yourself anyway).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yes. I'm saying while flight is theoretically an option, it's your worst option by far, even in a 1v1 scenario. </div> </div> </div>You're not saying why though. Retreating from a bad situation is frequently what a smart, thoughtful hunter should be doing; especially if things aren't going as planned.<br /> <br /> Killing a werewolf in Kuruth is a pain in the ass. Running away until it ends leaves you with either a free escape to go do something else, or stalking around and waiting for it to end, when you can do whatever you want to them as they pass out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sorry about not multiquoting you in responses, but I'm working via phone here, and am horribly too lazy to retype the information to do each section. Please forgive me for that. </div> </div> </div>Don't worry about it. Respond however works best for you. I multiquote mostly because it helps me process my responses more than any particular etiquette issue or some such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I understand your points, I just disagree with the premise. </div> </div> </div>OK, but what's the basis for the disagreement?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T03:38:59-07:00","id":1222195,"title":"","content":"If it doesn't have a mechanic, you've walked into Homebrew territory- balance goes out the metaphorical window. Perhaps in a night horrors book we can get the update we both want there.<br /> <br /> And yes I'm presuming equal pu for a number of reasons. If you're fighting 4pu over your head, and have no other advantage, either you've chosen the fight poorly, or your ST is jerking you around.<br /> <br /> We appear to have a different idea on how player agency and choices work. I'm a very sandbox style person, so if the player has found themselves in this situation, their own actions have lead them there. But j digress- this portion of the discussion appears no longer relavent.<br /> <br /> I might be mixing my conditions with 5e, but I don't have the books here to double check. I thought you specifically couldn't escape restrained.<br /> <br /> What else do you call winning in an RPG?<br /> <br /> And the basis is that if you go into a fight, and are outmatched by the opponent, running will be unlikely to net you a better result. Your in a room with a death raging werewolf because you wanted to be, the dm wanted you to be, or someone really really fucked up, and I hope you already have a plan for that.<br /> <br /> My premise is- if you don't have a plan to kill a pissed off pure when you walk into a room, you probably aren't leaving the room alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T14:33:07-07:00","id":1222307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178699-2e-uratha-in-death-rage-chasing-his-opponents?p=1222195#post1222195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it doesn't have a mechanic, you've walked into Homebrew territory- balance goes out the metaphorical window.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has mechanics... just 1e mechanics.<br /> <br /> And no, homebrew doesn't mean balance gets ignored. Lots of people on these forums are homebrews, and are very interested in designing things that appropriately fit into the games mechanically. A huge amount of homebrew stuff over in the WoD subforums are actually about cleaning up the poor balance of those game's rules.<br /> <br /> Hell, this whole thread is talking about homebrewing, because the WtF 2e mechanics don't directly interact with the CofD 2e core Chase rules and bodging them together is homebrew/ST calls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yes I'm presuming equal pu for a number of reasons. </div> </div> </div>But in actual play, PU isn't going to follow white-room considerations. PU 2 vs PU 3 is only &quot;fighting 1 over your head,&quot; and a smaller but still extant window of timing.<br /> <br /> And characters don't have &quot;Sense Primal Urge&quot; as a power to know exactly what the time window is with an opponent. &quot;They went Basu-Im first, so I clearly have a time advantage,&quot; isn't something characters have any reason to believe. It's a giant risk to take to assume a character has equal or less PU to you (and that there isn't anything further manipulating things around).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I might be mixing my conditions with 5e, but I don't have the books here to double check. I thought you specifically couldn't escape restrained. </div> </div> </div>The Restrain maneuver in grappling inflicts the Immobilized Tilt (explicit in 2e core, implied in WtF 2e core), which does allow for escape.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What else do you call winning in an RPG? </div> </div> </div>Having a good time playing out the story of your character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the basis is that if you go into a fight, and are outmatched by the opponent, running will be unlikely to net you a better result. </div> </div> </div>The initial situation wasn't predicated on &quot;going into a fight,&quot; but that a fight resulted.<br /> <br /> And whether or not running will net you a better result isn't something you can assert in a vacuum. There's too many variables... which allows the Chase system to be interesting in the first place. On top of the large number of stats that can play into things, there's a number of external situational factors, and tactics that can turn, &quot;this guy would beat me in a fair white-room fight,&quot; into, &quot;the odds are clearly in my favor to retreat.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is even more true as &quot;combat&quot; and &quot;chases&quot; have overlapping but not the same traits. A character can easily be better at you in combat, but worse in a chase, and vice versa. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My premise is- if you don't have a plan to kill a pissed off pure when you walk into a room, you probably aren't leaving the room alive. </div> </div> </div>And my premise includes that, it just also assumes that plans aren't always going to work out as intended. Plans aren't perfect, because character knowledge isn't perfect, and thus characters are inevitably going to be in situations they didn't plan for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T16:36:08-07:00","id":1222324,"title":"","content":"I think we're simply going to have to disagree. I actually had another long response typed up until I realized our primary difference is competency of players and playstyle. I'll bow out here and let things continue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}